From: AxelGalvez11 <axelgalvez1121@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 23:46:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] =?UTF-8?q?feat(nemesis-kit):=20round-29=20=E2=80=94?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20ChatGPT=20sources=20reading-list,=20sources=20open=20in=20ra?=
 =?UTF-8?q?il,=20updater=20neutered,=20thinking=20phrases,=20graph=20contr?=
 =?UTF-8?q?ols,=20study=20mind=20maps=20+=20tests,=20speed/breadth=20polic?=
 =?UTF-8?q?y?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Sources panel: rebuilt to ChatGPT's vertical reading-list anatomy (publisher
  line + real fetched article title + domain), split Citations / Also consulted;
  click reads in the rail's own Browser tab (no separate Chrome), hover ↗ =
  external; error-page titles (400/403 from raw API URLs) never shown.
Rail: fullscreen toggle (Esc exits); native view follows placeholder.
Recorder: short-viewport compaction so the record button stays on screen at zoom.
Thinking preview: live one-line activity phrases (activity-phrase.ts, 22 tests).
Graph: rotationSpeed slider + showNames + neighborGlow toggles (persisted).
Study: per-section MIND MAPS (markmap viewer) + PRACTICE TESTS (take-test flow,
  scoring, miss review, attempts) — agent-created as Library/Mindmaps/*.md +
  Library/Tests/*.json; extras.ts + 26 tests (55 total green). Verified live.
Self-updater: student About page no longer offers the git-pull update (it tracked
  upstream Hermes main and rebuilt stock over the fork — twice-confirmed cause of
  the repo resets); updates.json pinned to our branch.
Agent policy (SOUL): simple Q = seconds w/ one lookup; research = many searches
  fired together (2-4 PubMed + web_search), 10-20 candidates, cite 6-12;
  web_search for non-clinical/current-events lookups.
Fast/Thinking answer modes already existed in the composer (no build).
